<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Máximo Gómez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a>–<a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Máximo Gómez was a Dominican-born general who became the commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>'s independence armies. He fought throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> of 1868–1878 and, as general-in-chief in the war of 1895, led the invasion of western Cuba with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-maceo">Antonio Maceo</a>, using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> tactics and the burning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> estates. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a> in 1905, after Cuban independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximo-gomez.jpg" alt="Máximo Gómez" width="302" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MaximoGomezBaez2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
